From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kirill <sleeply4cat@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 01:59:27 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 12/27] ASoC: codecs: wcd937x-sdw: don't overrun the channel
 tables

The binding requires 12 tx-channel-mapping values, counting dmic7, but
the codec has no dmic7 and wcd937x_sdw_tx_ch_info has 11 entries. Probe
writes all 12, past the end of the table and into whatever follows it.

Here that was HPH_L's ch_mask in the RX table: it became 8, which the
hardware drops, so only the right channel was enabled on the HPH port.

Bound both loops by the table size.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015ya7egg5XM6dMvKwj1kAyq
---
 sound/soc/codecs/wcd937x-sdw.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/wcd937x-sdw.c b/sound/soc/codecs/wcd937x-sdw.c
index 1ad75c226..568bac4b5 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/wcd937x-sdw.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/wcd937x-sdw.c
@@ -1024,6 +1024,10 @@ static int wcd9370_probe(struct sdw_slave *pdev,
 		pdev->prop.src_dpn_prop = wcd937x_dpn_prop;
 		wcd->ch_info = &wcd937x_sdw_tx_ch_info[0];
 
+		/* The binding counts dmic7, which this codec doesn't have. */
+		master_ch_mask_size = min_t(int, master_ch_mask_size,
+					    ARRAY_SIZE(wcd937x_sdw_tx_ch_info));
+
 		for (i = 0; i < master_ch_mask_size; i++)
 			wcd->ch_info[i].master_ch_mask = WCD937X_SWRM_CH_MASK(master_ch_mask[i]);
 
@@ -1041,6 +1045,9 @@ static int wcd9370_probe(struct sdw_slave *pdev,
 		pdev->prop.sink_dpn_prop = wcd937x_dpn_prop;
 		wcd->ch_info = &wcd937x_sdw_rx_ch_info[0];
 
+		master_ch_mask_size = min_t(int, master_ch_mask_size,
+					    ARRAY_SIZE(wcd937x_sdw_rx_ch_info));
+
 		for (i = 0; i < master_ch_mask_size; i++)
 			wcd->ch_info[i].master_ch_mask = WCD937X_SWRM_CH_MASK(master_ch_mask[i]);
 	}
